id: pm-jhpby4
title: "ADR: Ordering assurance partitions evidence-cited blocks from uncited blocks"
description: "Authorize three simultaneous blocks ratchets: retain the historical total ceiling as an outer bound, preserve the anti-fabrication ceiling over non-evidence rows, and floor evidence-cited ordering."
type: Decision
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-20T20:11:18.429Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T22:08:27.637Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T21:39:30.278Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T21:39:30.278Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The existing blocks ceiling is retargeted to total blocks minus evidence-cited blocks; Evidence-cited blocks receive an independent non-regression floor; Both assertions carry executable boundary negative controls and remain blocking in graph-composition; The historical total blocks ceiling remains a blocking outer bound with adjacent pass and fail controls
goal: Provable history
objective: Keep anti-fabrication and recovered ordering simultaneously enforceable
value: Evidence-backed historical ordering can grow without weakening graph governance
impact: Unblocks pm-c90tfh and its three ordering-lineage dependents
outcome: Provenance-partitioned blocking assertions replace one contradictory global count
why_now: The live global blocks ceiling is exactly saturated and rejected the required evidence-backed edges
parent: pm-m2u1
resolution: "Accepted ADR: retain the historical total blocks outer ceiling, preserve the uncited ceiling, and independently floor evidence-cited blocks."
expected_result: Total ordering-edge growth stays bounded; uncited directional-edge growth cannot spend evidence headroom; and recovered evidence cannot be silently removed.
actual_result: "The historical total ceiling was 243. The current graph measures total blocks=205, comprising uncited=202 and evidence-cited=3; blocks-total-ceiling retains 243 as the outer bound, blocks-ceiling enforces the current uncited ceiling of 202, and the evidence floor protects all 3 recovered edges."
