close_reason: "Accepted after review: the ADR now consistently retains total=243 as an outer bound while independently enforcing uncited=202 and evidence-cited>=3."
body: "## Context\nThe historical blocking assertion counted all blocks rows identically and carried a total ceiling of 243. Accepted graph reconstruction also requires evidence-backed ordering edges, so one undifferentiated ratchet could not express all required properties.\n\n## Decision\nRetain the historical total ceiling of 243 as a blocking outer bound. Define evidence-cited blocks by the explicit evidence: source-kind prefix. Define uncited blocks as total minus evidence-cited. Move the anti-fabrication ratchet to the uncited population at its current ceiling of 202 and add a floor of 3 over evidence-cited rows. All three assertions remain blocking and carry adjacent pass/fail negative controls.\n\n## Consequences\nTotal ordering edges cannot grow beyond the historical bound without a new Decision. Adding an evidence-cited ordering edge cannot spend anti-fabrication headroom. Deleting recovered ordering fails the evidence floor. Adding a block without evidence provenance fails the uncited ceiling. Changing any population requires a verified Decision."
